## The legal move

Both surfaces end in `TryPlace`, so the pointer and the terminal can never
disagree. A move is refused, **by name**, when:

- the piece is already there
- the place is a readout and the hand tried to drop into it (a log is produced
  by a command, not filled in)
- the place does not accept that kind of piece
- the place requires the piece to have been somewhere else first

## What it raises

| event | when | what binds to it |
|---|---|---|
| `OnPiecePlaced(groupId)` | a piece is legally placed for the FIRST time | a `collect` objective — one count per piece |
| `OnGroupComplete(groupId)` | every piece of a group is placed | an objective counted once |
| `OnZoneFilled(zoneId)` | every piece a place accepts is in it | a `reach` objective |
| `OnCommand(verb)` | a declared command ran and did something | an `interact` objective |
| `OnRejected(reason)` | an illegal move, with the text the player saw | anything that wants to react to a mistake |

`OnPiecePlaced` fires on first placement only. A mission that counted every
shuffle back and forth would complete on one piece being dragged in and out.

